WHY I READ THESE AS GENUINE, NOT BACKFILLED
- Ordering: every red predates its own green by minutes, and all of them
  (17:26-17:48) predate all four W-016 commits (d80ba3f 17:50:51, 37c3aec
  17:51:12, a6f92f8 17:51:38, 30b540c 17:51:57).
- Provenance: every stack trace names
  .claude/worktrees/wf_f8104331-3d7-2/... — builder-a's per-builder worktree,
  which was pruned before round 2 ran at 18:10. These cannot have been produced
  after the fact; the tree they were produced in no longer exists.
- Internal consistency: each red's failure mode is the exact pre-fix state of
  the symbol its commit introduces (store.on, isPathContained,
  ClaudeCodeHooksOpts.sella, the cwd redaction, the unused import), and its
  green twin shows those same named assertions passing. A fabricated red does
  not line up symbol-by-symbol with the diff that follows it.
The lex Sec.2/Sec.7 contract is "the test has been run and shown failing, and
that failure is kept as evidence". Substance met: captured before the fix,
kept, inspectable, and re-inspectable now. Round 2's finding was correct on the
facts round 2 had (it searched studio/ci/, the worktrees and .bisellium/); it
is wrong on the facts as they now stand.

ESCALATED REGARDLESS (mechanism, not this opus)
The reds live outside the officina because the officina sanctions no
per-behaviour red store: opera front matter has no redEvidence slot, verify
mints only the three automated gate logs, and nothing in studio/ references
/tmp or ~/.bisellium-evidence. So this evidence is honest but not durable
studio evidence — a mtime-dated file tree a reviewer must be told about is not
a certificate. Stays escalated to the Patron: the fix is a CLI-minted red store
(a redEvidence slot per behaviour, written by the tool, certifying the tree the
red was taken in), not a convention about where builders drop logs. This is the
third recurrence of lesson class review x evidence-backfilled-or-absent
(L-001, L-008); it is a tooling gap, and round 3 shows the builders were doing
the right thing with nowhere sanctioned to put it.

